  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skilled youth and adult for a green and prosperous Eastern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Eastern Africa, there are needs and requests from Member States for development of youth and adult skills through TVET, youth literacy and adult education to meet the needs of individuals, the labor market and society. The population, specially youth, must be equipped with skills that will enable them to tackle specific challenges that the region faces, such as the high rates of (i) poverty (ii) informal sector, (iii) populations with low levels of literacy and skills, (vi) young population without decent job, and (v) migrants and refugees. To address these challenges, UNESCO will support Member States to develop technical and vocational skills, literacy and numeracy for youth and adults.</narrative>
  </description>
